From 6993c08b5b260b908ae2a2a9e27c390361e58263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:02:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(indoor): owner-reviewed boundary patches as a
 regeneration source review

A master with applied but unregenerated boundary patches is not a
regeneration input. saveNativeBoundaryPatches(apply=true) adds tagged wall
faces and drops the prepared circulation geometry, so the unchanged graph's
native-cell floor aliases (e.g. a room arrival to a ramp landing walk) can no
longer be proved and readIndoorProject refuses the master. The October 21
source reviews also bind the original dataset and rooms bytes.

regenerate-from-native-cache.ts gains --boundary-patch-review,
--applied-boundary-patch-master and --boundary-patch-supersessions. The
input master stays the unchanged source. The patch file is re-imported into
it with importNativeBoundaryPatchFile (exact evidence), and the applied
master that the project's own application wrote from the same source is
checked to differ only by exactly those rows (status applied) and the listed
contact repairs (applied to restored). The rows then join the reviewed
source rooms after the door aperture review; the compiler consumes them and
refuses any applied patch it cannot compile. A receipt and the portable
review files are written next to the other replays. run.sh passes the
options through optional environment variables; unset, the command is
unchanged.

